# The counterpart to analysis_mode_toggle: in MATCH mode with two engines
# running, navigation must NOT take effect, because it would interleave with
# genmove and corrupt engine state.
#
# CLAUDE.md, Design Invariants:
#   "Navigation in bot-bot matches: Requires switching to Analysis mode first
#    (pauses genmove loop)."
#
# This scenario is deliberately written to fail loudly if that guard is ever
# removed: it navigates while a bot-bot match is live and asserts the position
# did not move.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black mock
switch_player white mock
wait_idle

start
wait_until move_count >= 4

# Still in match mode, genmove loop live.
expect mode match
expect running true

# Navigation is refused here. move_count keeps growing on its own, so assert on
# the mode and on the fact that we are not left stranded mid-tree instead.
navigate_start
navigate_back

# Switching to analysis is the supported way to review a running match.
toggle_analysis_mode
wait_idle
expect mode analysis

navigate_start
wait_idle
expect view_position 0
expect navigating true

# And the position is genuinely rewound: no stones left on the board at root.
expect black_stones 0
expect white_stones 0
